# /owasp-review -- On-Demand Security Audit

## When to Use

Invoke `/owasp-review` before merging any feature that touches:

- Authentication or authorization logic
- File I/O or path handling
- Subprocess execution (`child_process`, shell invocations)
- External HTTP calls or API integrations
- Dependency updates (`package.json`, `package-lock.json`)
- Template rendering with user-controlled input
- Configuration loading from external sources
{{- if .IsInternal }}
- Stripe webhook signature verification
- JWT token validation or session management
- RabbitMQ message handling or queue configuration
{{- end }}

## Invocation

```bash
/owasp-review
```

Spawns the `security-reviewer` agent against `git diff main...HEAD`. The agent runs the full 6-step Investigation Protocol and produces a `SECURITY_APPROVED` or `SECURITY_BLOCKED` verdict.

---

## OWASP Top 10:2025 Reference

| ID | Name | What to Check |
|----|------|---------------|
| A01 | Broken Access Control | Deny by default. Enforce authorization server-side. Verify object ownership. |
| A02 | Security Misconfiguration | Harden configs. Disable debug/defaults in production. Use Helmet.js. |
| A03 | Software Supply Chain Failures | Lock dependency versions. Audit with `npm audit`. |
| A04 | Cryptographic Failures | TLS 1.2+. `crypto.randomBytes` not `Math.random`. |
| A05 | Injection | Prisma parameterized queries. No `eval()`. Validate input with Joi/Zod. |
| A06 | Insecure Design | Threat model critical flows. Rate limit with express-rate-limit. |
| A07 | Authentication Failures | Secure session management. Rate limit auth endpoints. |
| A08 | Integrity Failures | Verify upstream integrity. Safe JSON parsing. |
| A09 | Logging Failures | Log security events. No sensitive data in logs. |
| A10 | Exception Handling | Fail-closed. Hide internals from users. |

